[{"text":"CSPD[p, q] is the D-1-dimensional scalar product of p with q and is transformed into CartesianPair[CartesianMomentum[p, D-1],CartesianMomentum[q, D-1]] by FeynCalcInternal.","anchor":"cspd"},{"text":"CSPD[p] is the same as CSPD[p,p] (=p^2).","anchor":"cspd"},{"text":"Overview, SPD, ScalarProduct, CartesianScalarProduct.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"CSPD[p, q] + CSPD[q]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[p\\cdot q+q^2\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CSPD[p - q, q + 2 p]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[(p-q)\\cdot (2 p+q)\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ExpandScalarProduct[ CSPD[p - q, q + 2 p] ]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-p\\cdot q+2 p^2-q^2\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ExpandScalarProduct[CSPD[p - q]]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-2 (p\\cdot q)+p^2+q^2\\]","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CSPD[a, b] // StandardForm (*CSPD[a, b]*)","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CSPD[a, b] // FCI // StandardForm (*CartesianPair[CartesianMomentum[a, -1 + D], CartesianMomentum[b, -1 + D]]*)","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CSPD[a, b] // FCI // FCE // StandardForm (*CSPD[a, b]*)","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCE[ChangeDimension[CSP[p, q], D]] // StandardForm (*CSPD[p, q]*)","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"}]